---
// Camlock Applications — 买家工况组织
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Camlock Applications — Agriculture, Chemical, Fuel, Food and Marine"
  description="Camlock couplings in agriculture irrigation, chemical transfer, fuel delivery, food &amp; beverage, marine, water and IBC bulk handling — the right material and type for the duty."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Applications"
    subtitle="Camlock couplings in agriculture, chemical, fuel, food, marine and bulk handling — the right material, type and gasket for the duty."
    breadcrumb={{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Applications' }}
  />
  <section class="cp-section">
    <div class="kv-container">
      <article class="cp-prose">
        <h2>Applications</h2>
        <p>Camlock selection starts with the duty: what is being transferred, at what pressure and temperature, and how often the line is connected and disconnected. From that, the material, the type letter and the gasket compound follow.</p>
        <h3>Agriculture &amp; Irrigation</h3>
        <p>Water and liquid fertilizer transfer for pivots, drip and flood irrigation. Aluminum couplings with EPDM gaskets cover most farm duties; polypropylene for fertigation chemicals.</p>
        <h3>Chemical Transfer</h3>
        <p>Acid, solvent and chemical loading and unloading with polypropylene or 316 stainless couplings and Viton or PTFE gaskets — compatibility checked at service temperature, not from a generic chart.</p>
        <h3>Fuel &amp; Oil Transfer</h3>
        <p>Gasoline, diesel, lube and hydraulic oil lines. Brass couplings where spark risk and thread strength matter; aluminum with NBR gaskets for standard fuel transfer.</p>
        <h3>Food &amp; Beverage</h3>
        <p>Sanitary transfer of milk, juice, beer, wine and edible oils with 304/316 stainless couplings and food-grade EPDM or silicone gaskets that stand up to washdown and CIP cycles.</p>
        <h3>Marine &amp; Offshore</h3>
        <p>Saltwater, ballast and deck wash systems with 316 stainless or aluminum couplings and marine-grade gaskets. Tool-free hookup keeps crew time short.</p>
        <h3>Water, Dewatering &amp; Fire</h3>
        <p>Site water, dewatering, fire-fighting and municipal connections where a quick, tool-free coupling on a suction or delivery line saves hours.</p>
        <h3>IBC &amp; Bulk Handling</h3>
        <p>IBC tote, tanker and drum connections for bulk chemical and food transfer — threaded adapters and camlock-to-sanitary transitions keep totes on standard 2&quot; thread.</p>
        <p>For a specific duty — fluid, pressure, temperature and connection size — send us the operating conditions and we will come back with coupling options and figures.</p>
        <h2>Next step</h2>
        <p>Send your duty conditions, or browse the coupling ranges and selection guides first.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="cp-cta">
        <a href="/contact/" class="kv-btn kv-btn--primary kv-btn--lg kv-btn--block-mobile">Request a Quote</a>
        <a href="/products/" class="kv-btn kv-btn--outline kv-btn--lg kv-btn--block-mobile">Browse Coupling Ranges</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cp-section { padding: 4rem 0; }
  .cp-prose { max-width: 52rem; }
  .cp-prose h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .cp-prose h3 { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .cp-prose p { color: var(--color-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .cp-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.875rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
